<section aria-labelledby="h-search-tips" class="help-search-tips" id="search-tips">
<h2 class="help-search-tips__heading" id="h-search-tips">Search Tips</h2>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Here are some tips to help you to easily find collection items.</p>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-basic-search">Basic Search</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">The search box searches everything. This is the best place to start.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Start with a basic keyword search using two or three keywords. Search failures can result from over-specifying the search.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Things to try when you're getting irrelevant or too many results</p>
<ul class="help-search-tips__list">
<li class="help-search-tips__list-item">Add more words.</li>
<li class="help-search-tips__list-item">Use the dropdown when a common word is pulling in results you don't want.</li>
</ul>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">The dropdown beside the search box lets you restrict your search to a single part of the record:</p>
<div class="help-search-tips__group help-search-tips__group--v2">
<strong class="help-search-tips__strong help-search-tips__strong--v1">Dropdown option</strong><span class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v3">Searches</span>
<strong class="help-search-tips__strong help-search-tips__strong--v2">All Fields</strong><span class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v4">The whole record</span>
<strong class="help-search-tips__strong help-search-tips__strong--v1">Title</strong><span class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v3">Title only</span>
<strong class="help-search-tips__strong help-search-tips__strong--v2">Creator</strong><span class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v4">Creator names only</span>
<strong class="help-search-tips__strong help-search-tips__strong--v1">Subject</strong><span class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v3">Subject headings only</span>
</div>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">For example, searching `Melbourne` in All Fields returns anything mentioning Melbourne anywhere; searching it under Title returns only items with Melbourne in the title.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Suggestions appear as you type. These are drawn from terms that exist in the catalogue, so picking one guarantees you'll get results.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Type any combination of title, creator, date, place, or subject terms. All your keywords will appear in a record. This is an AND search.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">The best matches will be in the first two pages of the search results.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Results are ranked by their relevance to your search terms, based on:</p>
<ul class="help-search-tips__list">
<li class="help-search-tips__list-item">where the words appear in the record (words in the title, or creator are ranked the highest)</li>
<li class="help-search-tips__list-item">number of occurrences of the term within the record</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-faceted-search">Faceted Search</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">The filter terms in Faceted Search allow you to refine your search results by presenting structured and extended data (format type, collection, date ranges, and subject) and the number of results per field grouping (images – 2,000). If your result set is large, review the filters to see what Format, Creators, or Subjects are represented. Select appropriate filters to view only the most relevant to your query.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Because filters depend on the item metadata, they might not be a complete representation of all the collection items available. These are under continuous review and update to provide the more powerful filters.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Once you select a field limit, it remains in effect until you remove it. That is, if you enter a new search using the Basic Search box the results will be limited by the selected values.</p>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-refining-results">Refining results</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Active filters appear as chips above the results. Remove a chip to drop that filter or choose Clear all to start again. Sort by relevance, date or title, and switch between grid and list views.</p>
<div class="help-search-tips__group help-search-tips__group--v1">
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Collection.</strong> Limit the list of results to include only the holdings of a specific collection. New collections and items are increasingly being made available.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Date.</strong> A histogram shows the distribution of your results by year, decade, or century, depending on the size of the range. To narrow the date range of your results, use the slider, or enter a start and end year, and click Apply.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Creator.</strong> Artists, Authors, Collectors, Designers, Manufacturers, and contributors to works in your results. Disambiguating a creator's name from hundreds of results by using the filter and select from among the list - full name or birth/death dates - to only see the one/s you want.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Organization (as Creator).</strong> Corporate or government entities that are identified as creator or are otherwise responsible for content.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Accession Number.</strong> Shows how your results are distributed across major disciplines. There are several standards used. Most common is uses a prefix acronym of the collection followed by the year of acquisition.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Object type.</strong> This is the category or physical format of the collection item. Use the search option to find all results for a particular type - for example, book, photograph, musical instrument, scientific equipment, or specimen.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Language.</strong> Select results created in or translated to a specific language.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Format.</strong> The digital format of works in your list of results – for example, image, pdf, audio, and video.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v2"><strong class="help-search-tips__text-strong">Access.</strong> Limit by works available online with a "Digital Asset", or physically 'On Access' or "On Display".</p>
</div>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-automatic-stemming">Automatic stemming</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Your search automatically includes plural and singular forms of your search terms, as well as common suffix and tense variations.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">For example: 'broad' will match records with the term 'broader' or 'broadest' but not 'broadly'</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Stemming applies within phrase searches as well as keyword searches.</p>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-truncation-wildcards">Truncation and wildcards</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Use an asterisk to truncate terms that aren't handled by stemming.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">For example, non-English variations - créat* will find création(s), créateur(s), créatrice(s), etc.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">You can truncate from the beginning as well - *science finds science, conscience, geoscience, omniscience.</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Use a question mark [?] to find variations of a single letter in a word - kvet?h will find kvetch or kvetsh.</p>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-exact-phrase">Exact phrase</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Use double quotation marks around your terms to match words in the exact order you typed them. For example, "architectural plan".</p>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-advanced-search">Advanced Search</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Want to search a single field — Title, Creator, Subject or Date range?</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Or to combine several fields use Contains all (AND), Contains any (OR) or Does not contain (NOT).</p>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">Use advanced search when you need to:</p>
<ul class="help-search-tips__list">
<li class="help-search-tips__list-item">combine two or more specific fields</li>
<li class="help-search-tips__list-item">combine two or more values of a limit</li>
<li class="help-search-tips__list-item">items in two select collections</li>
</ul>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">The results will not include the term if they appear in unselected fields. Basic search will return results across all fields but the items you are looking for may not be ranked highly.</p>
<h3 class="help-search-tips__heading-boolean">Boolean</h3>
<p class="help-search-tips__text help-search-tips__text--v1">You can create complex Boolean logic using AND, OR, and NOT (all in upper-case) and parentheses for nesting.</p></section><aside aria-labelledby="h-contact-box-topic" class="contact-box">
